<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="50670" href="schedule/2023/spring/CMN/496/50670.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2023" href="schedule/2023.xml">2023</calendarYear><term id="120231" href="schedule/2023/spring.xml">Spring 2023</term><subject id="CMN" href="schedule/2023/spring/CMN.xml">Communication</subject><course id="496" href="schedule/2023/spring/CMN/496.xml">Adv Topics in Communication</course></parents><sectionNumber>JYU</sectionNumber><sectionTitle>Intro Communication Analytics</sectionTitle><creditHours>3 hours</creditHours><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>This course covers basic skills of analyzing quantitative and qualitative data from the internet, social media, and survey. Students will learn basics of R programming and how to use R for data manipulation, statistical analysis, and data visualization. These skills provide an overview of communication analytics, and they also serve as a necessary foundation for students interested in learning advanced computational methods and data science in communication.</sectionText><sectionNotes>Restricted to Undergrad - Urbana-Champaign.</sectionNotes><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>CrossListOpen (Restricted)</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2023-01-17Z</startDate><endDate>2023-05-03Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="S9 ">Lecture-Discussion</type><start>12:30 PM</start><end>01:50 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>TR     </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>1026</roomNumber><buildingName>Lincoln Hall</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Yang" firstName="J">Yang, J</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>